## Why does Google hold financial content to a higher standard?

Google holds financial content to a higher standard because wrong money advice can harm readers. Google calls these "Your Money or Your Life" (YMYL) topics. Pensions, investments, mortgages and tax planning all fall inside that group.

The definition comes from Google's [Search Quality Rater Guidelines](https://services.google.com/fh/files/misc/hsw-sqrg.pdf). Raters are asked to look for stronger evidence of experience, expertise and trust on YMYL pages.

The guidelines are not a ranking formula. They do show what Google wants its systems to reward. An advice firm shows this through named advisers, verifiable credentials, clear firm details and content that is accurate and current.

## How do FCA financial promotions rules affect SEO content?

FCA financial promotions rules can apply to your SEO content. The rules cover communications that invite people to engage in financial activity. Web pages, blog posts and social content can all fall within scope.

The FCA sets out the detail on its [financial promotions](https://www.fca.org.uk/firms/financial-promotions-adverts) page. Promotions must be fair, clear and not misleading.

I am not a compliance adviser and I do not give regulatory advice. Every page I draft or edit goes through your firm's own compliance sign-off before it is published. My job is to make that sign-off easy: clear drafts, tracked changes and a record of what was approved and when.

## What ranks for "financial adviser near me"?

Local searches show a map pack above the organic results. Getting into it depends on a few connected signals.

- **Google Business Profile:** the right primary category, accurate address and hours, services listed and photos of the real office and team.
- **Reviews:** a steady flow of genuine client reviews on Google. Any review request process should be checked by compliance first.
- **Adviser profile pages:** one page per adviser with their FCA register number. Each page links to the adviser's entry on the [FCA register](https://register.fca.org.uk/s/). This lets a reader and a search engine confirm the person is authorised.
- **Consistent citations:** the same firm name, address and phone number on adviser directories such as unbiased and VouchedFor, professional body listings and the main UK business directories.
- **Office or town pages:** a page for each office with real local detail. Thin copies of the same page with the town name swapped add little.

Firms with several offices usually need [local SEO](/services/local-seo/) work before anything else.

## How do adviser bio pages support E-E-A-T?

Adviser bio pages support E-E-A-T by showing the qualified person behind the advice. Clients buy advice from people. Search engines and AI assistants also look for a named author. A strong adviser page includes qualifications such as Chartered or Certified status, areas of advice, years in practice, the FCA register link and articles the adviser wrote or reviewed.

Each article should name its author or reviewer and link to that bio. This connects your content to a real, checkable expert. My guide to [E-E-A-T in SEO](/blog/what-is-eeat-seo/) covers the wider signals.

## Which topic clusters work for financial planning firms?

Pensions, inheritance tax, retirement planning and mortgages are the clusters that suit most financial planning firms. Topic clusters group a main guide with supporting pages on narrower questions. They help a firm show depth on the subjects clients actually ask about.

| Cluster | Example supporting pages |
|---|---|
| Pensions | Consolidating old pensions, drawdown versus annuity, pension transfer advice |
| Inheritance tax | Gifting rules, trusts, estate planning for business owners |
| Retirement planning | When you can retire, income planning, state pension timing |
| Mortgages | First-time buyer process, remortgage timing, buy-to-let basics |

Each page should answer the question plainly. It should then explain when professional advice is worth getting. A [topical map](/services/topical-maps/) plans the full set before writing starts. Figures such as tax allowances change. Every page needs a review date.

## How do AI assistants answer money questions?

AI assistants answer money questions by drawing on pages they can read and trust. Those pages include your site, directories and press coverage. Some people now ask ChatGPT, Copilot, Perplexity and Google's AI Overviews about pensions, tax and choosing an adviser.

You cannot control what an AI assistant says. Answers vary from one run to the next. You can make sure your firm's facts are clear, consistent and easy to find across the web. The [AI visibility audit](/ai-visibility/) checks agreed buyer questions across the available AI search tools and benchmarks your firm against three agreed competitors. That gives you a baseline before changing anything. Schema markup helps search engines read a page. It is not a way to get cited.

## What does a compliance-aware content workflow look like?

This is the workflow I use for regulated content. Your compliance team owns step 5.

1. **Agree the topic and search intent:** which question the page answers and who it is for.
2. **Brief the adviser:** a short call or written notes so the content reflects real practice.
3. **Draft the page:** plain English, sources linked, no outcome promises.
4. **Add required wording:** risk warnings and disclosures your firm already uses.
5. **Compliance sign-off:** your team reviews, edits and approves the final text.
6. **Publish and record:** the approved version goes live with the approval date logged.
7. **Review on a schedule:** pages with tax figures or rules are checked again at each tax year or rule change.

